WEBVTT

01:31.080 --> 01:33.920
<b>May 6th, Midnight</b>

01:34.380 --> 01:36.960
We got home earlier than I thought we would!

01:37.170 --> 01:37.750
Mm-hmm.

01:38.920 --> 01:40.040
<b>SHIGA TRAIN DERAILMENT</b>

01:38.920 --> 01:40.040
<b>Recovery efforts continue</b>

01:39.130 --> 01:44.670
Recovery efforts continue
after a train derailment in Shiga Prefecture.

01:40.040 --> 01:42.420
<b>SHIGA TRAIN DERAILMENT</b>

01:40.040 --> 01:42.420
<b>Recovery efforts continue</b>

01:43.670 --> 01:44.790
<b>SHIGA TRAIN DERAILMENT</b>

01:43.670 --> 01:44.790
<b>Recovery efforts continue</b>

01:45.330 --> 01:48.420
This footage from immediately after the accident
shows the extent of the derailment,

01:48.420 --> 01:52.830
as rescue workers hurry to extract
injured survivors from the train.

01:53.580 --> 01:55.670
While little information on the cause...

01:56.420 --> 01:59.830
Eiko... I saw Ai, lying there unconscious.

02:00.170 --> 02:00.830
What?!

02:03.000 --> 02:04.830
Sorry to call so late, Keitaro.

02:05.170 --> 02:08.540
It's okay. Is what you texted me really true?

02:08.830 --> 02:12.670
Yeah. Ai was on the train that derailed in Shiga.

02:13.290 --> 02:18.500
The accident was the result of a battle...
between Ai's god and the Spectre of Death.

02:19.630 --> 02:26.500
Ai's god protects her, so she should be uninjured,
but there are too many red flags here.

02:27.250 --> 02:29.540
So, we need to go check in on Ai.

02:30.460 --> 02:32.630
We need to go to Kyoto.

02:33.920 --> 02:37.170
Wait, Yayoi-chan, today was
the last day of Golden Week.

02:37.790 --> 02:45.500
You've got school, and while Eiko and I
can skip classes, you can't miss days at school.

02:45.710 --> 02:47.710
Why should I care about school when my friend's-?

02:50.040 --> 02:52.290
Never mind. Keitaro's right.

02:53.670 --> 02:55.040
Sorry. Just forget it.

02:55.460 --> 02:56.920
Y..Yayoi-chan...

02:58.540 --> 03:00.630
Did she just... Give up on that?

03:00.630 --> 03:07.330
I think she feels pressured to stay on top of school,
thinking she owes us for taking her in.

03:08.540 --> 03:10.580
She has every right to be worried,

03:10.790 --> 03:14.920
especially when Ai-chan's her friend,
and the Spectre's responsible for her parents' deaths...

03:15.580 --> 03:18.250
Eiko, can you free up your weekend?

03:18.420 --> 03:19.000
Huh?

03:19.460 --> 03:24.500
When Ai-chan's parents call the tutoring center,
I'll ask about visiting her.

03:25.000 --> 03:25.790
Sounds good!

03:26.880 --> 03:33.830
As we quietly prepared for a trip to Kyoto,
our Golden Week of horrors came to an end.

03:41.000 --> 03:44.380
Ai's god won the battle, then healed the Spectre.

03:45.290 --> 03:49.830
It's much, much stronger than I imagined,
and it's a split spirit, too.

03:50.250 --> 03:54.170
And why did the God heal it? Just how powerful is it?

03:55.330 --> 03:57.250
What will the Spectre do next?

03:58.130 --> 03:59.380
But above all, will Ai be okay?

04:00.380 --> 04:04.250
I wonder if there's any way to get school
to stop happening for a while...

04:04.670 --> 04:06.960
Good morning, Hozuki-san!

04:08.880 --> 04:09.710
Who're you?

04:09.710 --> 04:15.210
My, it's been a while since you came to our school!
I thought you would remember me!

04:15.750 --> 04:18.580
I'm in the class next to you! My name is Dorothy.

04:19.080 --> 04:20.830
Dorothy Flamsteed.

04:21.880 --> 04:24.920
I'll come right out with it: you have the sight, don't you?

04:27.130 --> 04:29.040
I do, too, you see.

04:30.210 --> 04:31.830
So, Hozuki-san...

04:32.750 --> 04:36.710
Would you care to learn more
about the places that are haunted here?

04:40.290 --> 04:41.750
You mean, at our school?

04:42.330 --> 04:43.170
Yes!

04:45.580 --> 04:51.080
Someone removed the spirit
from the Old I Watergate and took the arm, too?

04:51.420 --> 04:59.250
Yes, a team of three people, and one was
a little girl in grade school, or so I've been told.

05:00.710 --> 05:04.750
A little girl? Could she be gifted, too?

05:05.170 --> 05:07.540
I might know who she is.

05:08.040 --> 05:11.250
This body seems to have known her.

05:12.630 --> 05:15.040
She was terrified of her.

05:16.830 --> 05:22.920
She always carried an extremely dangerous spirit
with her, like none she'd ever seen.

05:23.580 --> 05:27.790
To make things worse,
she was constantly surrounded by evil spirits.

05:29.830 --> 05:37.080
I'll get to the bottom of things,
find out if she has the arm, or any powerful abilities.

05:38.000 --> 05:39.750
She may be of use to us.

05:41.170 --> 05:43.460
You can see something in my doll, right?

05:44.040 --> 05:46.790
With so much in common, we're sure to become friends!

05:47.080 --> 05:52.540
So, why don't we begin our budding friendship
by exploring these schoolyard haunts?

05:53.790 --> 05:57.500
Sure, but none of the ghosts
are school are particularly powerful.

05:58.500 --> 05:59.630
Unless you know of one?

05:59.710 --> 06:01.000
As a matter of fact, I do!

06:01.750 --> 06:05.040
I borrowed this faculty key
and made a copy of it for myself.

06:05.250 --> 06:10.790
There's a ghost in the midst of a dramatic transformation.
Shall we go see it together?

06:12.540 --> 06:15.330
As long as you don't tell me what to do, then sure.

06:15.750 --> 06:16.830
Oh, yay!

06:17.170 --> 06:19.790
Then let's reconvene after school!

06:20.420 --> 06:24.380
What do you get out of this? Thinking of exorcising it?

06:27.960 --> 06:29.920
I should keep an eye on her.

06:33.580 --> 06:36.170
Let's see what you're capable of.

06:39.670 --> 06:44.170
I looked into the stories about our school,
but they all turned out to be made up.

06:41.290 --> 06:42.960
<b>CHATDG: Tell me about the scary stories</b>

06:41.290 --> 06:42.960
<b>at Tokikodai Elementary.</b>

06:45.170 --> 06:48.420
There you are again, zoning out on your phone all alone!

06:49.630 --> 06:51.790
You're gonna end up with no friends, Yayoi-chan!

06:50.380 --> 06:51.920
<b>Class Rep:</b>

06:50.380 --> 06:51.920
<b>Yoko Nakiri</b>

06:50.380 --> 06:51.920
<b>Nickname: Rep</b>

06:52.290 --> 06:55.330
Rep, just leave her alone...

06:52.380 --> 06:55.130
<b>Classmate:</b>

06:52.380 --> 06:55.130
<b>Futaba Sasaki</b>

06:52.380 --> 06:55.130
<b>Nickname: Fuu-tan</b>

06:55.130 --> 06:56.250
<b>Classmate:</b>

06:55.130 --> 06:56.250
<b>Aki Hocchi</b>

06:55.130 --> 06:56.250
<b>Nickname: Ahocchi</b>

06:55.420 --> 06:56.330
Yeah!

06:56.420 --> 06:57.540
I'm researching something.

06:57.880 --> 06:59.580
You're always researching something!

06:59.880 --> 07:05.540
Speaking of, have you guys heard about
the seven ghosts at our school?

07:06.460 --> 07:07.960
Reading about scary stories?

07:08.130 --> 07:12.080
Wow, Hozuki, you seriously believe in ghosts?

07:10.040 --> 07:12.540
<b>Classmate:</b>

07:10.040 --> 07:12.540
<b>Daisuke Gonda</b>

07:10.040 --> 07:12.540
<b>Nickname: Dai-chan</b>

07:12.250 --> 07:13.830
What are you, five?!

07:14.330 --> 07:17.750
What, you wanna go? Let's take this outside.

07:17.750 --> 07:20.380
To do what, exactly?!

07:20.500 --> 07:22.170
Prove who's tougher.

07:22.330 --> 07:23.830
You sure you're not friends?

07:24.330 --> 07:26.580
Whatever. It's on, Hozuki!

07:26.580 --> 07:27.540
This'll be a bloodbath.

07:27.540 --> 07:28.960
C'mon, guys!

07:29.750 --> 07:34.540
Well, then! Why don't we go and see
if these ghosts really do exist?

07:36.710 --> 07:39.170
Wait, you're in the class next door.

07:39.170 --> 07:40.380
Dorothy, right?

07:40.920 --> 07:46.460
You were arguing about believing in ghosts, yes?
Then let's find out if they do!

07:47.130 --> 07:50.420
You wouldn't bow out of a challenge like this, would you?

07:50.420 --> 07:52.330
O-of course not!

07:52.330 --> 07:53.790
R-really?

07:53.960 --> 07:56.420
It's better than them duking it out...

07:56.790 --> 07:58.540
And it should be fun. Let's do it.

07:58.540 --> 07:59.420
Huh?!

07:59.670 --> 08:01.210
What's she plotting?

08:02.130 --> 08:04.250
You sure this is okay, Yayoi-chan?

08:04.580 --> 08:05.630
Don't see why not.

08:05.920 --> 08:08.790
Then let's all meet together after school!

08:08.790 --> 08:09.830
O-okay.

08:11.040 --> 08:13.790
I don't remember her acting like this before.

08:14.080 --> 08:17.250
Back in second grade, she was way shyer...

08:21.040 --> 08:23.170
I bet there are no ghosts!

08:23.790 --> 08:24.960
Then I bet that there are.

08:25.960 --> 08:29.420
So what ghosts are haunting our school, anyway?

08:29.710 --> 08:34.670
All I've seen are a few wandering ghosts
that are close to disappearing, but...

08:34.750 --> 08:39.210
Allow me to tell you about the seven ghosts
haunting Tokikodai Elementary!

08:40.580 --> 08:44.420
First, we have Hanako-san in the toilet,

08:44.670 --> 08:49.630
then, a Mona Lisa painting with moving eyes;
a thirteeth step that shouldn't be there;

08:49.830 --> 08:55.170
an unplugged phone in the gym that still rings;
a pool that pulls you in by your feet;

08:55.330 --> 08:58.330
a secret locked room;
and the sobbing ghost of a teacher.

08:59.290 --> 09:01.960
Perhaps we could visit them all in order!

09:02.670 --> 09:04.540
Or maybe we shouldn't...

09:04.540 --> 09:08.000
Don't worry. I'll keep you safe.

09:08.210 --> 09:10.540
Yayoi-chan's so cool...

09:12.710 --> 09:14.460
Here's the first ghost,

09:15.830 --> 09:20.580
who lives in the far left stall
of the girls' bathroom on the third floor.

09:21.210 --> 09:23.330
Knock three times and ask...

09:23.500 --> 09:25.420
Hanako-san, are you in there?

09:25.710 --> 09:30.380
...and she might just give you an answer!

09:37.290 --> 09:40.210
Well, whaddya know. Nothing happened.

09:40.420 --> 09:43.630
Sheesh, this was a huge waste of time!

09:45.710 --> 09:47.250
Nothing's here! Right?

10:07.960 --> 10:10.080
We haven't seen a single ghost!

10:10.330 --> 10:13.210
The only ones left are the secret room
and the crying teacher.

10:14.170 --> 10:17.670
Why'd you bring up these seven ghosts in the first place?

10:17.880 --> 10:21.830
Worried about your little bet? Then you needn't fret.

10:22.000 --> 10:24.210
You must have seen the markings by now.

10:24.630 --> 10:28.040
All seven locations are leading spirits
down a particular path.

10:28.290 --> 10:31.460
We're bound to see something, I know it!

10:32.290 --> 10:34.080
And I know exactly where to go.

10:35.040 --> 10:42.080
I asked how she'd keep everyone safe,
but I don't know if she's planning on doing that.

10:43.210 --> 10:50.830
The key probably opens up that locked room...
where Dorothy knows something is going to happen.

10:53.920 --> 10:57.380
The paths are converging, bringing the spirits together...

11:07.580 --> 11:09.710
This the secret locked room?

11:10.330 --> 11:12.170
Yes, and this here is the key!

11:12.380 --> 11:14.000
Wait, you want me to do it?!

11:14.500 --> 11:18.000
I was hoping someone courageous could help me...

11:18.420 --> 11:19.880
Then, I guess I'll help!

11:22.170 --> 11:25.830
Hozuki-san, do you know what "satsugo" means?

11:26.040 --> 11:28.040
I don't. What is it?

11:28.580 --> 11:32.790
It's from a Chinese novel called
"The Investiture of the Gods."

11:33.250 --> 11:40.460
In it, there is an enlightened monk who has renounced
all desires, save for one he cannot conquer:

11:40.830 --> 11:43.380
the desire to kill.

11:43.580 --> 11:47.500
<b>SATSUGO</b>

11:43.750 --> 11:47.040
That "desire to kill" is called "satsugo."

11:47.880 --> 11:52.380
These nearly-disappeared ghosts on the path
appear to have no lingering attachments,

11:52.380 --> 11:54.960
but they do still have some lingering satsugo.

11:55.290 --> 11:57.130
How'd you figure that out?

11:57.130 --> 11:58.920
Oh, it was easy!

11:59.500 --> 12:03.290
I carved symbols to change the path the spirits took,

12:03.290 --> 12:06.960
forcing them to converge at one particular point.

12:07.710 --> 12:08.960
Do you know what happened?

12:11.000 --> 12:15.420
The wandering ghosts consumed one another!

12:16.130 --> 12:19.830
Despite being incredibly weak,
and having no lingering attachments whatsoever!

12:20.920 --> 12:24.880
So, I've been putting together
this little experiment for a while.

12:26.040 --> 12:31.500
What would happen if the wandering spirits
are sent to a ghost with a vicious grudge?

12:32.330 --> 12:36.250
I could create a spirit
with an unslakable thirst for murder!

12:36.920 --> 12:40.290
All the paths in the school lead spirits
to the locked room.

12:40.830 --> 12:43.750
That's right! All that's left is to open it!

12:45.670 --> 12:46.500
Got it unlocked!

12:46.500 --> 12:47.250
No, don't!

12:47.380 --> 12:49.210
Everyone, run away from that door!

13:27.380 --> 13:29.630
Where am I...?

13:34.420 --> 13:35.210
Who was it?

13:35.330 --> 13:37.330
<b>DIE</b>

13:35.330 --> 13:37.330
<b>IDIOT</b>

13:35.340 --> 13:37.330
<b>PISS OFF</b>

13:35.340 --> 13:37.330
<b>CREEP</b>

13:35.340 --> 13:37.330
<b>PEDO</b>

13:37.750 --> 13:39.880
Who did this?

13:40.250 --> 13:42.460
The sobbing ghost of a teacher.

13:44.830 --> 13:45.880
These must be...

13:52.130 --> 13:53.380
Little brats.

13:56.170 --> 13:58.080
...the teacher's memories.

14:09.040 --> 14:10.000
I'm sure of it.

14:11.580 --> 14:15.880
Sakashita-sensei! Taking lewd photos
of a student without her consent?!

14:16.290 --> 14:17.750
I didn't do that-

14:17.750 --> 14:19.830
The pictures were on your phone!

14:20.080 --> 14:24.000
I'm appalled! There's no excuse for this!
Fess up immediately!

14:29.580 --> 14:32.080
<b>DIVORCE PETITION</b>

14:35.000 --> 14:36.500
You disgust me.

14:40.080 --> 14:45.670
I didn't... do anything.

14:47.460 --> 14:49.830
So did he actually take those pedo photos?

14:49.830 --> 14:55.790
Of course he didn't. He doesn't lock his phone,
so it was super easy to take some as "evidence."

14:55.880 --> 14:58.330
Yikes. Poor guy.

15:19.750 --> 15:22.750
<b>MAY THESE DEMON CHILDREN</b>

15:19.750 --> 15:22.750
<b>SUFFER FOR THEIR CRIMES</b>

15:30.080 --> 15:35.710
His ghost was so close to disappearing
that I left him alone.

15:36.080 --> 15:36.750
But...

15:37.460 --> 15:40.750
now that his desire to kill has been refueled,
he's gone completely berserk.

15:41.250 --> 15:42.630
Thanks to a certain someone.

15:47.790 --> 15:53.380
Ready or not, here I come... To kill you.

15:53.630 --> 15:54.580
Sensei...

16:03.790 --> 16:07.880
Will everyone be able to escape, I wonder?

16:08.540 --> 16:10.830
From this nightmarish game of hide and seek.

16:20.420 --> 16:25.830
Wh-what the hell?! Everyone's gone,
it's dark, and then there was that monster...

16:25.830 --> 16:27.500
Why is this happening?!

16:52.630 --> 16:53.420
He's here!

17:15.080 --> 17:16.290
That was so scary!

17:27.170 --> 17:29.670
Found you.

18:04.920 --> 18:12.580
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry...

18:12.750 --> 18:19.580
Hozuki-san, if you can escape this game,
and do something about this forlorn teacher,

18:20.130 --> 18:22.000
I'll call this your win.

18:24.080 --> 18:27.540
But will you truly be able to rescue them all?

18:28.750 --> 18:34.500
Ready or not, here I come... To kill you.

18:44.750 --> 18:49.830
If you want to kill me,
you'd better move quicker and quieter, Sensei.

18:51.500 --> 18:53.250
That was way too easy.

18:53.920 --> 18:56.630
He must have created this ghostly school.

18:57.000 --> 19:00.500
If I take him out, I should be able to get out of it.

19:05.080 --> 19:06.330
But nothing's happening.

19:08.250 --> 19:11.040
Ready or not, here I come...

19:14.290 --> 19:19.130
His wounds are healing,
though I know that part of him was consumed.

19:19.830 --> 19:23.080
Are there multiple teachers? No, that's unlikely.

19:23.710 --> 19:29.380
Or maybe he'll always regenerate,
as long as he's within this parallel space he created.

19:30.170 --> 19:33.210
Ready or not, here I come...

19:33.630 --> 19:43.330
And it sounds like he's following the rules
of hide and seek, only cursing me if he finds me.

19:44.630 --> 19:46.460
What would happen then?

19:49.540 --> 19:51.380
What's going on?!

19:52.380 --> 19:55.290
I ran out of the school to get away from that creepy thing,

19:55.750 --> 19:58.290
but the second I left, I was running back
in through the back entrance!

19:59.290 --> 20:00.290
And then...

20:04.790 --> 20:08.080
...when it blew out the candle...

20:10.880 --> 20:14.580
...something horrible happened to Gonda!

20:16.580 --> 20:23.880
I thought no one was here, but maybe if I leave
and come back in, I'll find someone again!

20:24.630 --> 20:28.080
I need to find someone who can help me!

20:32.170 --> 20:33.000
Yayoi-chan?!

20:33.460 --> 20:34.880
And the creepy thing!

20:36.250 --> 20:40.880
Wh-what just happened?!
I don't know, I don't wanna know!

20:40.500 --> 20:41.380
<b>YAYOI-CHAN</b>

20:43.540 --> 20:46.170
There's no way my phone will work here...

20:46.500 --> 20:50.880
I-it's gonna be okay.
Yayoi-chan just took care of him, right?

20:51.380 --> 20:53.460
Yayoi-chan!

20:53.830 --> 20:54.630
Is that Rep?

20:59.290 --> 21:01.290
I'll kill it and be right there!

21:01.830 --> 21:02.380
<b>YAYOI-CHAN</b>

21:03.710 --> 21:06.250
Hello? Yayoi-chan?! I-it went through?!

21:06.460 --> 21:10.960
That you, Rep? Thank God. Let's meet up.

21:11.080 --> 21:14.830
Yes, please! Where should we meet up?

21:15.330 --> 21:18.880
I'm on the third floor. Can you meet me
at the stairs by the shoe lockers?

21:19.130 --> 21:20.250
Y-yeah!

21:20.790 --> 21:21.500
Okay, bye.

21:21.500 --> 21:23.130
Wait! Don't hang up!

21:24.000 --> 21:26.330
I'm really scared. Can you stay on the phone with me?

21:26.830 --> 21:28.790
Sure. What should we talk about?

21:29.670 --> 21:32.330
I know. What's your favorite flower?

21:32.580 --> 21:33.540
Flower?

21:33.750 --> 21:36.830
I love dandelions! What about you?

21:37.330 --> 21:41.830
I don't really have a favorite, but I hate funeral lilies.

21:43.040 --> 21:46.790
O-oh, okay. Wh-what's your next question?

21:46.960 --> 21:49.540
What do you use more often, a box cutter, or scissors?

21:49.920 --> 21:52.630
Huh? Uh, probably scissors?

21:52.830 --> 21:54.580
Are you good at throwing rocks at people?

21:54.710 --> 21:58.130
No, of course I'm not good at that!
I've never thrown a rock at anyone!

21:58.130 --> 22:01.880
What about scratching cars, or telling lies?

22:02.290 --> 22:05.290
Wait, what? Why're you asking me this, Yayoi-chan?

22:05.290 --> 22:10.000
One last question.
What's the worst thing you've ever done?

22:11.880 --> 22:14.380
I ditched after school tutoring once...

22:14.580 --> 22:15.540
You're lying.

22:16.000 --> 22:18.830
What? N-no, I'm not...

22:39.920 --> 22:47.210
The worst thing you did was faking
nasty pictures and ruining a man's life.

22:47.670 --> 22:52.960
Your little antics drove him to kill himself.
Don't you remember?

22:53.750 --> 22:57.880
H-hey... Yayoi-chan, i-is that you, or...

23:07.000 --> 23:09.630
Found you.

23:11.670 --> 23:17.330
NO!

23:22.750 --> 23:28.710
Yayoi fights to escape the ghostly school
that's trapped her and her classmates.

23:29.790 --> 23:37.920
When she discovers the culprit is a spirit that's replaced
a human soul, she makes plans for her counterattack.
